  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Psalms",
    "delineation": "Psalm",
    "number": 32,
    "summary": "David says, Blessed is the man unto whom the Lord imputes not iniquity—David acknowledges his sin—He recommends that the righteous be glad in the Lord and rejoice.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Blessed is he whose transgression is forgiven, whose sin is covered.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 7,
            "text": "JST Ps. 32:1 Blessed are they whose transgressions are forgiven, and who have no sins to be covered. Rom. 4:7 (7–8)."
          },
          {
            "start": 20,
            "end": 33,
            "text": "TG Sin; Transgress."
          },
          {
            "start": 37,
            "end": 45,
            "text": "TG Remission of Sins."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 19
          },
          {
            "start": 34,
            "end": 36
          },
          {
            "start": 47,
            "end": 52
          },
          {
            "start": 57,
            "end": 59
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Blessed is the man unto whom the Lord imputeth not iniquity, and in whose spirit there is no guile.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 93,
            "end": 98,
            "text": "TG Guile; Sincere."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 8,
            "end": 10
          },
          {
            "start": 81,
            "end": 89
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "When I kept silence, my bones waxed old through my roaring all the day long.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For day and night thy hand was heavy upon me: my moisture is turned into the drought of summer. Selah.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 72,
            "text": "IE strength dried up as."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I acknowledged my sin unto thee, and mine iniquity have I not hid. I said, I will confess my transgressions unto the Lord; and thou forgavest the iniquity of my sin. Selah.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 82,
            "end": 89,
            "text": "TG Confession."
          },
          {
            "start": 93,
            "end": 107,
            "text": "TG Transgress."
          },
          {
            "start": 132,
            "end": 141,
            "text": "TG Forgive."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "For this shall every one that is godly pray unto thee in a time when thou mayest be found: surely in the floods of great waters they shall not come nigh unto him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 38,
            "text": "TG Godliness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Thou art my hiding place; thou shalt preserve me from trouble; thou shalt compass me about with songs of deliverance. Selah.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 12,
            "end": 24,
            "text": "Ps. 91:1; 119:114."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 8
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I will instruct thee and teach thee in the way which thou shalt go: I will guide thee with mine eye.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 25,
            "end": 30,
            "text": "TG Teaching."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Be ye not as the horse, or as the mule, which have no understanding: whose mouth must be held in with bit and bridle, lest they come near unto thee.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 24,
            "end": 26
          },
          {
            "start": 40,
            "end": 45
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Many sorrows shall be to the wicked: but he that trusteth in the Lord, mercy shall compass him about.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 5,
            "end": 12,
            "text": "Prov. 13:21; Rom. 2:9; Alma 41:10; D&C 1:3. TG Despair."
          },
          {
            "start": 49,
            "end": 57,
            "text": "TG Trust in God."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 13,
            "end": 21
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Be glad in the Lord, and rejoice, ye righteous: and shout for joy, all ye that are upright in heart.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 82
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
